        {
          "type": "reasoning",
          "text": "Implement stable_unique: iterate, use a list for seen and equality check via `in` (which uses ==). For efficiency with hashables we could use a set, but unhashables must work. Simple approach: keep a list `result`, check `any(item == x for x in result)`. Careful: `x in result` uses equality, works. But NaN edge cases — equality-based is fine per spec.\n\nOptimize: maintain a set for hashable items and list for unhashable. Simpler robust approach:\n\ndef stable_unique(values):\n    result = []\n    seen_hashable = set()\n    unhashables = []\n    for v in values:\n        try:\n            h = hash(v)\n        except TypeError:\n            if not any(v == u for u in unhashables):\n                unhashables.append(v)\n                result.append(v)\n        else:\n            if v not in seen_hashable:\n                seen_hashable.add(v)\n                result.append(v)\n    return result\n\nNote: a value could be equal to a hashable one but unhashable? Unlikely; equality between hashable and unhashable different types is rare (e.g., custom classes). Acceptable.\n\nEdge: hash(v) may succeed but v not hashable for set? No, hash works means set works. NaN: hash fine, set membership: nan != nan so duplicates kept — that's equality semantics, fine.\n\nReplace the raise with implementation.",
          "time": {
            "start": 1790854655649,
            "end": 1790854665245
          },
          "id": "prt_0f7416ea1001qn5mYS3FMVsxl1",
          "sessionID": "ses_f08bed584ffeutrzPF57B04YPC",
          "messageID": "msg_0f7415cea001eiQGOwEpMZdlfm"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "{\"action\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"sequences.py\",\"old\":\"def stable_unique(values):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Keep the first occurrence of each equality-distinct value.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    raise NotImplementedError(\\\"stable_unique\\\")\",\"new\":\"def stable_unique(values):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Keep the first occurrence of each equality-distinct value.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    result = []\\n    seen_hashable = set()\\n    seen_unhashable = []\\n    for item in values:\\n        try:\\n            hash(item)\\n        except TypeError:\\n            if not any(item == other for other in seen_unhashable):\\n                seen_unhashable.append(item)\\n                result.append(item)\\n        else:\\n            if item not in seen_hashable:\\n                seen_hashable.add(item)\\n                result.append(item)\\n    return result\"}",
